From 40a2db7a56422a0d7de58fcd176fecc4d61fd322 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:45:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] centroid_aspect check: wider tolerance for clusters with
 spread aspects

Mini-batch k-means centres are not exactly the mean of their pixels: for a
cluster whose aspects are spread (centre shorter than 0.7), the direction
of (aspect_sin, aspect_cos) and the circular mean of the pixels differ by
up to ~20 deg on the Davos example (1 cluster in 300), which the check
reported as an error. Such clusters are compared within 45 deg; the
arithmetic-mean bug the check targets gives errors near 180 deg.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012FMkEYDUJxvxmd3SbUsJfP
